## Answer Format Rules

| Question type | Format | Example |
|--------------|--------|---------|
| Single number | digits only, no commas/$ | `2273.8` |
| Percentage | number + % | `12.34%` |
| Slope + intercept | [s, i] with brackets + comma | `[0.123, -234.567]` |
| Two sub-answers | [a, b] with brackets + comma | `[1234567, 12.34%]` |

- Thousand-separator commas are stripped by `write_answer` — no need to remove them.
- Never add units (millions, billions, dollars) inside the answer string.
- `round()` uses conventional half-up rounding (0.5 → up), NOT Python's banker's rounding.
- Round only the FINAL result — never round intermediate values.
- Always use `calculate()` for arithmetic — never compute in your head.

